  "correction_rules": [
    "Reduce forecast overshoots after sharp price spikes (e.g., >75% of forecasted value) by 10-15% to avoid overreaction.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias correction: if forecast is >20% above recent 7-day average, reduce by 5-10%.",
    "For sentiment = 0.00, assume neutral market, apply no bias; if sentiment > 0.00, slightly increase forecast to reflect bullish bias.",
    "If true outcome is consistently below forecast (e.g., 3 consecutive days), reduce next forecast by 5-8% to avoid overestimation.",
    "For long-term (30d) forecasts, apply a 3-5% downward adjustment if historical 30d mean is below 70.00 to account for downward drift.",
    "If forecast peaks early and then drops, reduce subsequent forecast by 5-10% to reflect potential correction."
  ]
}
